  "recording": {
    "maritime": "Direct MediaRecorder capture of the rendered canvas; silent WebM transcoded to H.264 MP4, variable frame timing retained, padded by at most one pixel to even dimensions. No interpolated motion. Browser capture has uneven frame cadence; encoded duration is reported per file. The recorder requests twenty seconds; frames can begin late under load.",
    "coastalWatch": "Existing 15 October recording: 634 screenshots encoded with capture intervals at 30 output fps. 10.85 seconds of uncaptured gaps removed with direct cuts; UI clocks may jump. Silent. No fabricated observations.",
    "screenshots": "JPEG browser screenshots. Earlier captures were copied without image changes; their incorrect .png suffixes were corrected to .jpg. Current proxy captures include the local recording controls."
  },
  "boundaries": [
    "Maritime study positions are fixed. Weather and sea use nearby FMI observations where available; defaults remain for missing fields. This is not live voyage footage.",
    "Night footage depicts 19:00 UTC while retaining the current morning weather observations. It is a lighting study, not a weather forecast.",
    "Architecture is reference-informed, with simplified facade spacing, roof profiles and illustrative background heights and finishes.",
    "Coastal watch tracks and alerts are synthetic. It does not run the track-fusion pipeline.",
    "Earlier maritime screenshots predate this capture session; their precise commits are not asserted.",
    "No client, operator, voyage or result is implied. Nothing was supplied by the ship or its operator."
  ],
